WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.160
What happens if we introduce Dr.&nbsp;
Gears’ pocket watch to the Clockworks?

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.800
Four clockwork pocket watches, belonging&nbsp;
to Dr. Gears, were prepared for testing.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.520
First, a gold-plated watch was placed in&nbsp;
914 on the setting “Fine.” It produced a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.400
small clockwork bird that, when its tail was&nbsp;
pressed, emitted the sound of a robin’s call.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.760
Next, another identical watch was&nbsp;
run through the machine on “Fine.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.440
This time, it produced a small toy&nbsp;
train engine, powered by clockwork.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.400
The next watch run through&nbsp;
on “Fine” emerged as a tiny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.240
fully functional grandfather clock&nbsp;
set to Eastern Standard Time.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.360
The final watch produced a little&nbsp;
metal sculpture of a piano.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.320
Though each watch was placed&nbsp;
in 914 on the same setting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.160
and was made from the same materials,&nbsp;
they all produced a different result.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.840
The only common thread was the&nbsp;
metal and the presence of clockwork.

